[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Chromium (nitro)
GenericName=Web Browser
Comment=Chromium on nitro's Ozone backend (software rendering)
# Installed only by `just deploy-chromium`, never by `just deploy`: this
# file lives in `deploy/chromium/` rather than `deploy/` precisely so the
# `deploy/*.desktop` glob in `deploy-bins` cannot pick it up and put a
# launcher entry on a box that has no Chromium build.
#
# `Exec=` is the bare name of a wrapper script, not the browser, for the
# same reason `nitro-term.desktop` is bare: the launcher spawns without a
# shell and does not expand `~` or `$HOME`, and `nitro-session` prepends
# `~/nitro-bin` to every child's `PATH` (#3723). The wrapper
# (`deploy/chromium/chromium-nitro`, installed as
# `~/nitro-bin/chromium-nitro`) supplies the flags and the profile dir.
Exec=chromium-nitro %U
# The file name, the window's app id and this key are the same string,
# `chromium-nitro`, on purpose. The wrapper passes `--class=chromium-nitro`,
# which Chromium's nitro backend sends as `SetAppId`; the launcher asks the
# server for this file's basename; and the server resolves an app id first
# in the icon theme — where `just deploy-chromium` installs Chromium's own
# logo as `hicolor/<N>x<N>/apps/chromium-nitro.png` under
# `~/.local/share/icons` — and then through `<app_id>.desktop`'s `Icon=`.
# So launcher row, bar entry and title bar all land on the same PNG.
Icon=chromium-nitro
Terminal=false
StartupWMClass=chromium-nitro
Categories=Network;WebBrowser;
Keywords=browser;web;internet;chromium;
MimeType=text/html;x-scheme-handler/http;x-scheme-handler/https;
